# Squash solo - Ladder: Figure of Eight
@description The figure of eight in fifteen levels, from front-wall hits with a bounce to the full
  corner volley drill. Based on The Pursuit of Squash.
@speech rate 1.1
@minimum gap 0:00.8
@workout squash
@artwork ../images/squash.jpg
@include ../shared/squash.overtone

## Intro
Figure of eight ladder. Play the chapter for your level and repeat it until you reach the target,
then move on to the next. After a miss, count from zero.

// The Pursuit of Squash, Figure 8 Progressions. Levels 1 and 2 are front wall only; from level 3 each
// shot goes into a front corner, front wall then side wall.
## Level 1: Front wall, one bounce
@ladder
Front wall, one bounce. Stand just in front of the T, facing the front wall. Front wall only:
forehand across to your backhand, backhand back across, with one bounce between hits. A blue or red
dot ball helps.
+0:00.7 Target: one hundred without a break.
+0:00.7 Watch the ball onto the strings.
+0:00.7 Stay relaxed. This one is focus.

## Level 2: Front wall volleys
@ladder
Front wall volleys. Same place, front wall only, forehand to backhand, now on the volley with no
bounce. A blue or red dot ball helps.
+0:00.7 Target: one hundred without a break.
+0:00.7 Short swings. Racket up between hits.
+0:00.7 Keep it above the service line.

## Level 3A: Forehand into the corner
@ladder
Forehand into the corner. Stand on the T. Forehand into the front wall near the left corner, so it
goes on into the side wall and comes straight back to you. Catch it, and go again.
+0:00.7 Target: twenty-five without a break.
+0:00.7 Front wall first, then the side wall.
+0:00.7 Lands in front of you? Aim further from the side wall.

## Level 3B: Backhand into the corner
@ladder
Backhand into the corner. On the T. Backhand into the front wall near the right corner, so it goes
on into the side wall and comes straight back to you. Catch it, and go again.
+0:00.7 Target: twenty-five without a break.
+0:00.7 Front wall first, then the side wall.
+0:00.7 Lands behind you? Aim closer to the side wall.

## Level 4A: One figure of eight, forehand first
@ladder
One figure of eight, forehand first. On the T. Forehand into the front left corner, let it bounce
once, then backhand into the front right corner. Catch it, and go again.
+0:00.7 Target: twenty-five without a break.
+0:00.7 Racket up as soon as you've hit.
+0:00.7 Same spot on the front wall each time.

## Level 4B: One figure of eight, backhand first
@ladder
One figure of eight, backhand first. On the T. Backhand into the front right corner, let it bounce
once, then forehand into the front left corner. Catch it, and go again.
+0:00.7 Target: twenty-five without a break.
+0:00.7 Racket up as soon as you've hit.
+0:00.7 Same spot on the front wall each time.

## Level 5: Continuous, above the service line
@ladder
Continuous, above the service line. On the T. Forehand into the left corner above the service line,
one bounce, backhand into the right corner above the line, and keep it going without catching. Every
hit counts.
+0:00.7 Target: one hundred without a break.
+0:00.7 Above the line, both sides.
+0:00.7 Racket up between hits.

## Level 6A: Low forehand, high backhand
@ladder
Low forehand, high backhand. On the T, one bounce each. Forehand into the left corner below the
service line, backhand into the right corner above it, and keep it going.
+0:00.7 Target: twenty-five figure of eights without a break.
+0:00.7 Forehand low. Backhand high.
+0:00.7 Same swing. Only the height changes.

## Level 6B: Low backhand, high forehand
@ladder
Low backhand, high forehand. On the T, one bounce each. Backhand into the right corner below the
service line, forehand into the left corner above it, and keep it going.
+0:00.7 Target: twenty-five figure of eights without a break.
+0:00.7 Backhand low. Forehand high.
+0:00.7 Same swing. Only the height changes.

## Level 7: Both below the service line
@ladder
Both below the service line. On the T, one bounce each, both shots below the service line, so you
have less time. A single or double yellow dot ball.
+0:00.7 Target: twenty-five figure of eights without a break, each one a forehand and a backhand.
+0:00.7 Racket up early. Less time now.
+0:00.7 Stay on the T. Let the ball come.

## Level 8A: Adding the forehand volley
@ladder
Adding the forehand volley. On the T. Forehand into the left corner, one bounce, then lift your
backhand high into the right corner so it comes back to your forehand in the air. Volley it into the
left corner, and go again.
+0:00.7 Target: twenty-five without a break.
+0:00.7 Volley just above the service line.
+0:00.7 Lift the backhand. Give yourself time.

## Level 8B: Adding the backhand volley
@ladder
Adding the backhand volley. On the T. Backhand into the right corner, one bounce, then lift your
forehand high into the left corner so it comes back to your backhand in the air. Volley it into the
right corner, and go again.
+0:00.7 Target: twenty-five without a break.
+0:00.7 Rotate your forearm for power.
+0:00.7 Volley just above the service line.

## Level 9A: Volley start, forehand first
@ladder
Volley start, forehand first. On the T. Forehand into the front left corner, thirty centimetres from
the side wall. Before it bounces, volley it on your backhand into the right corner, then on your
forehand into the left. Stop there: that's one set.
+0:00.7 Target: ten sets without a break.
+0:00.7 Sweet spot. Let the racket do the work.
+0:00.7 In front of you? Further from the side wall. Behind you? Closer.

## Level 9B: Volley start, backhand first
@ladder
Volley start, backhand first. On the T. Backhand into the front right corner, thirty centimetres
from the side wall. Before it bounces, volley it on your forehand into the left corner, then on your
backhand into the right. Stop there: that's one set.
+0:00.7 Target: ten sets without a break.
+0:00.7 Sweet spot. Let the racket do the work.
+0:00.7 In front of you? Further from the side wall. Behind you? Closer.

## Level 10: The figure of eight
@ladder
The figure of eight. On the T. Start into a front corner, thirty centimetres from the side wall,
halfway between the service line and the out line. Then volley from corner to corner, front wall
first every time. Short of power on the backhand? Use a bouncier ball.
+0:00.7 Target: twenty volleys without a break.
+0:00.7 Front wall first, then the side wall.
+0:00.7 Sweet spot. Rotate your forearm on the backhand.
